==English==

===Etymology===
From {{suffix|en|breathe|er|pos2=[[agent noun]] suffix|id2=agent noun}} or {{suf|en||er|pos2=relational noun suffix|id2=relational}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/bɹiː.ðə(ɹ)/|a=UK}}
** {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-breather.wav|a=Southern England}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Wodencafe-breather.wav|a=US}}
* {{rhymes|en|iːðə(ɹ)|s=2}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# Something or someone that [[breathe]]s.
# {{lb|en|specifically}} A [[heavy breather]].
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=25 Apr 81|journal=Gay Community News|page=12|author=Martin H. Krieger|title=Phone Calls|text=Most of us make sense of the world through talk and sight, and '''breathers''' represent that most anxiety provoking experience, nothingness with a hint of possibility.}}
# {{C|en|Rest}} A short [[break]]; a [[rest]] or [[respite]].
#: {{ux|en|After a short '''breather''' she was ready to continue up the hill.}}
# {{lb|en|physics}} A [[spatially]] [[localized]], time-periodic [[excitation]] in a one-dimensional [[lattice]].
# {{lb|en|colloquial|dated}} That which puts one [[out of breath]], such as [[violent]] [[exercise]].
# {{lb|en|mechanics}} An air inlet path to the [[crankcase]]

